Hide official plugins listed in PASEO_ZCODE_SUPPRESSED_PLUGINS

Purpose: paseo-plugin-zcode-provider (ADR 19) runs ZCode in a standalone
Server that shares ~/.zcode with ZCode Desktop. Computer Use cannot start its
Helper there and Browser Use has no browser, yet the skills that Desktop
installed are still offered to the model. The provider lists such plugin IDs,
comma-separated, in PASEO_ZCODE_SUPPRESSED_PLUGINS. Discovery then skips them
the same way it skips suppressedBuiltins, without writing any configuration.

Target: NodePluginAdapter.discoverPluginsSync in
apps/zcode-cli/packages/adapters/src/plugins/index.ts, which every plugin
discovery path uses (ZCode 29628c9acdb81b703bbd4080c207a0e7ce5e276e).

Remove when: ZCode offers an official per-process way to hide official
plugins, for example when ZCODE_CUA_PRODUCT_HELPER=0 hides cached
computer-use as resolveOfficialPluginRoots says it should.

License: Apache-2.0, the license of the modified ZCode source.

